      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, for the cooling stage of cooked poultry, the temperature should be rapidly lowered from 63°C (145.4°F) to 21°C (70°F) within 2 hours, and then cooled to 5°C (41°F) or below within an additional 4 hours. Adhering to these stages is crucial for effectively reducing the risk posed by Clostridium perfringens.",
